# Supabase access

HSEQ Nova talks to Supabase **only** through:

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (browser, RLS, user session)
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (server, bypasses RLS)

Do **not** use `DATABASE_URL`, `DIRECT_URL`, `postgres://`, or the pooler host (`*.pooler.supabase.com`) against this project.

- Browser / user-scoped server: `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/client` or `@/lib/supabase/server` (anon).
- Server actions, webhooks, admin: `getAdminDb()` from `@/lib/supabase/admin` (service role).
- Prisma schema is types only. Never `prisma db push` against Supabase. Apply SQL from `supabase/migrations/` in the Supabase SQL editor.
